## Project overview (game systems)

This project is a Godot boss-rush style game with multiple playable characters. Character choice is stored globally, then the main scene applies stats, HUD, and per-class combat behavior.

### Runtime flow

1. **`main_menu.gd`** — Character roster lives in the `characters` array (`id`, `name`, `texture`, `desc`, `stats`, `abilities`). The chosen entry is copied into **`global.gd`** → `Global.player_class`.
2. **`main.gd`** — On `_ready`: applies **`Player1.apply_class_stats(...)`** from `Global.player_class`, sets the HUD avatar, wires **`Player1.setup_hud($HUD)`**, configures ability slot visibility/icons, and connects health updates.
3. **`player1.gd`** — The player `CharacterBody2D`: movement, dodge, i-frames, cooldowns, and all class-specific attacks. It asks **`CharacterCombat.id()`** (from `Global.player_class`) to decide behavior.

### Core scripts (high level)

| Script | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| **`character_data.gd`** (`CharacterData`) | Shared constants (e.g. ability id strings, stat min/max for ★ ratings on the class screen). |
| **`character_combat.gd`** (`CharacterCombat`) | Per-class data: current id, primary/secondary cooldowns, attack texture paths, secondary HUD icon, short loadout description. |
| **`player_animation_loader.gd`** (`PlayerAnimationLoader`) | Builds **`SpriteFrames`** for the player from PNG folders per character id (`run`, `idle`; Moon also gets `attack`). |
| **`player1.gd`** | Gameplay loop: physics; plays `run` / `idle`; dodge; primary/secondary per class (arrow, slashes, flask, fireball-style projectile, moon beam, neptune orb boost). |
| **`hud.gd`** | Hearts, minimap hooks, ability cooldown UI, character-specific secondary icon. |
| **`ability_cooldown_slot.gd`** | Circular cooldown + ability icon drawing for HUD slots. |
| **`swing.gd`** (with `swing.tscn`) | Melee slash hitbox spawned by the player (texture, damage, knockback, timing). |
| **`arrow.gd`**, **`poison_flask.gd`**, **`poison_cloud.gd`** | Venus primary / secondary / lingering hazard. |
| **`fireball.gd`** (`fireball.tscn`) | Mercury secondary (silver styling optional). |
| **`moon_laser.gd`** (`moon_laser.tscn`) | Moon secondary beam after channeling. |
| **`neptune_orb.gd`**, **`water_bolt.gd`** | Neptune companion orbit + auto-aim bolts; secondary triggers a temporary faster volley. |
| **`mob.gd`** | Enemy AI movement, knockback decay, knockback chaining (“bowling”); adds an ambient glow in `_ready`. |
| **`ambient_glow.gd`** + **`ambient_light_pool.gdshader`** | Reusable soft radial “light pool” (player/enemy auras). |
| **`dungeon_vignette.gdshader`** | Vignette-style shader (use depends on scene setup). |

### Where to change things

**Player animations (walk / idle / Moon attack)**  
- **Logic:** `player_animation_loader.gd` — folder paths per `character_id`, animation names, loop flags, `set_animation_speed`.  
- **Art:** `res://assets/player/...` (paths referenced in `PlayerAnimationLoader`).  
- **When they play:** `player1.gd` — `AnimatedSprite2D.play("run" | "idle" | "attack")`, run speed scale, Moon channel + `attack` then spawn `moon_laser`.

**Roster / class screen**  
- `main_menu.gd` — `characters` array: portraits (`texture`), stats, description text, ability list.

**Cooldowns, slash art, secondary HUD icon, tooltips**  
- `character_combat.gd` — `primary_cooldown`, `secondary_cooldown`, texture constants, `secondary_hud_icon_for`, `loadout_summary`.

**Melee hitbox feel**  
- `swing.gd` / `swing.tscn` and `_spawn_slash(...)` in `player1.gd` (damage, scales, knockback, duration).

**Projectiles / abilities**  
- `arrow.gd`, `poison_flask.gd`, `poison_cloud.gd`, `fireball.gd`, `moon_laser.gd`, `neptune_orb.gd`, `water_bolt.gd` and their `.tscn` files.

**HUD cooldown appearance**  
- `ability_cooldown_slot.gd`; layout in `hud.tscn` (ability slot nodes).

**Enemy animations**  
- `mob.gd` only plays `"run"` and flips the sprite; frame data lives on the Mob scene / its `SpriteFrames` resource in the editor.

### Globals

- **`global.gd`** — `Global.player_class` dictionary set from the main menu; read by main scene, player, and combat helpers.
